From: Mieczyslaw Nalewaj <namiltd@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 23:58:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: rtl8365mb: keep MAC6_SEL_SDS0 set on family D

On a TP-Link Archer AX55 v1 (IPQ5018 + RTL8367S-VB) the trunk reports
2.5Gbps/Full on both sides but moves no frames: the receiver never
asserts link (SDS 0x3d stays 0x0100 instead of 0x0111) and nothing
crosses in either direction, with no CRC, alignment or FIFO errors.

MAC6_SEL_SDS0 (bit 9 of SDS_MISC, 0x1D11) is set earlier in pcs_config()
with its own regmap_update_bits(), but the final update_bits at the end
of the function uses a mask that does not cover it, so it is cleared
again on the way out. Stock holds 0x0E12 there - the PA enables, the
mode field and bit 9 - so add bit 9 to the mask and value that are
written last.

Signed-off-by: Mieczyslaw Nalewaj <namiltd@yahoo.com>
[krics: dropped the 0x1D12 writes, that register does not decode; renamed
 the bit-9 reference to the existing MAC6_SEL_SDS0 define]
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
@@ -1522,9 +1527,11 @@ static int rtl8365mb_pcs_config(struct phylink_pcs *pcs, unsigned int neg_mode,
 
 		misc_mask = RTL8365MB_D_SDS_MISC_PA33PC_EN |
 			    RTL8365MB_D_SDS_MISC_PA12PC_EN |
-			    RTL8365MB_D_SDS_MISC_MODE_MASK;
+			    RTL8365MB_D_SDS_MISC_MODE_MASK |
+			    RTL8365MB_D_SDS_MISC_MAC6_SEL_SDS0;
 		misc_val  = RTL8365MB_D_SDS_MISC_PA33PC_EN |
-			    RTL8365MB_D_SDS_MISC_PA12PC_EN | sds_mode;
+			    RTL8365MB_D_SDS_MISC_PA12PC_EN | sds_mode |
+			    RTL8365MB_D_SDS_MISC_MAC6_SEL_SDS0;
 	} else {
 		/* Mux the SerDes to MAC8 in the requested mode */
 		misc_mask = RTL8365MB_SDS_MISC_MAC8_SEL_SGMII_MASK |
